<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Release (Developer ID, direct distribution) entitlements. Used by `scripts/build-app.sh release`, which signs
	     with the Hardened Runtime (`codesign -o runtime`). No App Sandbox (setDefaultApplication for tel: links fails
	     inside it, see docs/RELEASING.md) and no com.apple.security.get-task-allow (a release must not be debuggable).

	     Checked against Apple's documentation (2026-10-12):
	     - "Hardened Runtime" lists the resource-access entitlements a non-sandboxed hardened app may need: audio-input,
	       camera, location, addressbook, calendars, photos-library, apple-events. Contacts therefore needs
	       com.apple.security.personal-information.addressbook ("enable the Hardened Runtime capability and then
	       select Address Book"). The macOS privacy prompt still uses NSContactsUsageDescription.
	     - Bluetooth is NOT in that list: com.apple.security.device.bluetooth is an App Sandbox entitlement ("enable the
	       App Sandbox capability ... under Hardware, select Bluetooth"). A non-sandboxed hardened app reaches
	       IOBluetooth with the Bluetooth privacy permission (NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription), so the key is left
	       out here. To be confirmed on hardware with the first Developer ID build (docs/RELEASING.md, "Verification").
	     - The audio extension (phase 4) would add com.apple.security.device.audio-input; not before it ships. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.personal-information.addressbook</key><true/>
</dict>
</plist>
